# Python
#
# The build-artifact directory names here are ANCHORED to /python/. Unanchored, `lib/`
# matches a directory called `lib` at any depth -- which silently swallowed every future
# `ruby/lib/**` source file, `git add ruby/` included nothing, and the gem would have
# published empty. Same hazard for `build/`, `dist/` and `var/` in any other language.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.Python
env/
venv/
ENV/
/python/build/
/python/develop-eggs/
/python/dist/
/python/downloads/
/python/eggs/
/python/.eggs/
/python/lib/
/python/lib64/
/python/parts/
/python/sdist/
/python/var/
/python/wheels/
/python/*.so
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

